<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 130 0 R
/T (something no one asked for, but we wanted to push our limits even more. We decided to use zero molds and zero silicone tools. Everything had to be made 100% by hand. No shortcuts, no premade shapes, no support pieces. Just pure craftsmanship.)
/E (something no one asked for, but we wanted to push our limits even more. We decided to use zero molds and zero silicone tools. Everything had to be made 100% by hand. No shortcuts, no premade shapes, no support pieces. Just pure craftsmanship.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [11 12]
>>
endobj
292 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 130 0 R
/T (For the figurines, we created characters that represented Morocco from North to South. A Jebliya woman with her traditional clothing, holding her cat, symbolizing the North and the mountains of Tangier and Chefchaouen. A lion standing for the Middle Atlas, powerful and proud. A Sahraoui man representing the Sahara, carrying the identity and culture of the South. And at the base of the showpiece, camels walking across the desert, giving that final touch of authenticity.)
/E (For the figurines, we created characters that represented Morocco from North to South. A Jebliya woman with her traditional clothing, holding her cat, symbolizing the North and the mountains of Tangier and Chefchaouen. A lion standing for the Middle Atlas, powerful and proud. A Sahraoui man representing the Sahara, carrying the identity and culture of the South. And at the base of the showpiece, camels walking across the desert, giving that final touch of authenticity.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [13 14 15]
>>
endobj
